    "title": "‘American Idol’ Fans, There’s a New Way to Vote for Your Favorite Artists This Year",
    "text": "Ryan Seacrest's Net Worth Is Jaw-DroppingGood Housekeeping USLIVECurrent Time 0:00Total Duration 3:002 min readJump to:When can I vote for American Idol in 2026?How do I vote for American Idol in 2026?American Idol is partway through season 24—and wow, the talent has been incredible to watch!With new episodes airing every Monday night on ABC, longtime fans can watch the hopefuls compete for a chance at stardom. With Carrie Underwood, Luke Bryan, and Lionel Richie serving as judges, and the contestants putting their own spins on iconic songs, it’s time for the viewers to get involved in the process, too.If you’re interested in participating, here’s everything you need to know about how to vote for your favorite performers.When can I vote for American Idol in 2026?The voting portion of American Idol season 24 officially began March 16, 2026.Advertisement - Continue Reading BelowVoting for American Idol opens at the end of the show’s East Coast airing, which is approximately 10 p.m. ET/7 p.m. PT. Everyone can vote up to 10 times per voting method, and the window for voting officially closes at 6 a.m. ET/3 a.m. PT the following morning.Viewers can check the official American Idol website each week to find out when to vote. The show also recommends that folks check the FAQ page for updates throughout the season.Be sure to click \"save article\" at the top of this page so you have it handy when voting for American Idol season 24 opens.How do I vote for American Idol in 2026?American Idol has offered five different methods for fans to vote for their favorite artists. More on each below.How to vote for American Idol online:If you want to vote for American Idol via a computer or the internet browser of your choosing on your phone, you can go to the show’s official voting website to make your selection.Just an FYI, you’ll need to create a free account. Once you do, it’s super easy to sign in and choose the artist and how many times you want to cast your vote. But make sure to save all your choices, and remember—you only have 10 available votes with this method.How to vote for American Idol over text: All viewers need to do is text the number corresponding to the contestant to the number “21523.” Each contestant’s number will show on screen during their performance.How to vote for American Idol on social media: For the first time in American Idol history, the show is offering a new way for fans to vote. You can now choose which artist should move to the next round on social media—specifically Facebook, Instagram, and TikTok.An official pinned post will be available on American Idol’s social media accounts throughout the show, and fans can comment with the hopeful they’re voting for. Keep in mind you can only do one name per comment—but you can cast your vote up to a total of 10 times per finalist.",
